  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "dwg_free_MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA_private",
    "file": "libredwg/src/dwg.spec",
    "description": "The crash is a NULL/invalid pointer dereference during object cleanup of MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA. In the generated free routine (DWG_OBJECT block for MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA), the macro-expanded free path for AcDbAnnotScaleObjectContextData_fields/AcDbTextObjectContextData_fields frees/reads fields (notably handle/string-like members such as scale) without validating that the object was fully/validly initialized after malformed input parsing. With this PoV, corrupted object state reaches dwg_free(), and the private free function dereferences a wild high-value address at dwg.spec:9708.",
    "conditions": "Data flow: llvmfuzz feeds attacker-controlled bytes to DWG parser, which constructs an object typed as MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA from malformed content. Parsing leaves inconsistent/poisoned members in this object (especially members from AcDbAnnotScaleObjectContextData_fields / AcDbTextObjectContextData_fields). On teardown, dwg_free -> dwg_free_object -> dwg_free_variable_type -> dwg_free_variable_no_class dispatches to dwg_free_MTEXTATTRIBUTEOBJECTCONTEXTDATA, which calls the private free routine. Because free-time code assumes valid initialized members, it dereferences an invalid pointer and segfaults."
  },
